 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Deligne–Laumon direct-image bound",
 "statement": "Let $f_0:X_0\\to Y_0$ be a separated finite-type morphism of\n$k_0$-schemes, with $Y_0$ separated of finite type over $k_0$. For every\nconstructible Weil sheaf $F_0$ on $X_0$ that is $\\iota$-mixed of weights\nat most $w$, $R^rf_{0!}F_0$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w+r$\nfor every $r\\ge0$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf, order 3189"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-d-dl-general-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "First prove the assertion for every affine-line projection\n$\\pi_0:\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0}\\to Y_0$, by Noetherian induction on the base.\nOn a dense open of each integral component, stratify the source and\nuse a mixed filtration to reduce to pure sheaves lisse on their strata.\nA stratum dominating $Y_0$ is either an open in the relative line or\nhas generic relative dimension zero. After shrinking $Y_0$, the first\ncase is [sk-p-dl-general-relative-line] and the second is\n[sk-l-dl-general-quasifinite]. Nondominating strata disappear on this\nopen; the discarded part of the base is covered by induction.\nOpen–closed reduction restores the strata and filtrations.",
   "uses": [
    "sk-l-dl-general-quasifinite"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "For general $f_0$, use Noetherian induction and finite affine\nstratifications of source and target. Reduce to a dominant affine map\nof integral schemes, replacing the target by the closure of the image\nwhen necessary. By [sk-l-dl-general-normalization], its restriction\nover a dense open factors through a finite map and successive\naffine-line projections. The quasi-finite and composition lemmas apply\nto this factorization. The complements have smaller support and are\nrestored by [sk-l-dl-general-excision]. This proves the sheaf assertion.",
   "uses": [
    "sk-l-dl-general-normalization",
    "sk-l-dl-general-excision"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "sk-l-dl-general-quasifinite",
