  "statement": "Let $f:X_0\\to Y_0$ be separated of finite type and let $F$ be mixed\nof weights at most $w$. Then $R^if_!F$ is mixed of weights at most\n$w+i$ for every $i$.",
  "proof": [
   {
    "text": "We first show that the asserted property is stable under composition.\nFor $X_0\\xrightarrow{h}Z_0\\xrightarrow{g}Y_0$, consider the Leray\nspectral sequence for compact supports,\n\n$$\n E_2^{a,b}=R^ag_!(R^bh_!F)\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ R^{a+b}(gh)_!F.\n$$",
    "uses": [],
    "elementary": null
   },
   {
    "text": "It is Frobenius-equivariant by the naturality of the truncation tower\nand of the composition isomorphism for direct image with proper\nsupport ([sk-thm-sf-comp-composition]). If both maps have the asserted\nproperty, then $E_2^{a,b}$ has weights at most $w+a+b$. Each later\npage is a subquotient, and the abutment filtration, which is finite\nbecause the operations preserve bounded constructible complexes\n([sk-thm-sf-ctf-stability]), has the same bound in each total degree.",
    "uses": [],
    "elementary": null
   },
   {
    "text": "Now apply [sk-l-dl-general-normalization], refining the\npartitions to filtrations by open and closed pieces. On every refined\nsource piece, the first map is separated and quasi-finite, and so it\nhas the property by [sk-l-dl-general-quasifinite]; each projection of\na relative affine line has it by [sk-prop-wgen-relative-line].\nBy the composition argument, the map from the piece to $V$ has the\nproperty. Gluing on the source and on the target, with the exact\nsequence in each degree (the localization observation in the proof of\n[sk-prop-wgen-relative-line]), we reassemble the finite partitions. Since restrictions of $F$ keep\nits bound, this proves the assertion on $Y_0$.",
    "uses": [
     "sk-l-dl-general-normalization",
     "sk-l-dl-general-quasifinite"
    ],
    "elementary": false
   }
  ],
  "note": "the current blueprint (main-20261023-1620, weil-conjectures-blueprint 7284bb09da) states or proves this differently; a worker who touches the node follows it"
 }
